Review the payment form's submit journey. src/checkout/PayButton.tsx:22-27:
```tsx
const onSubmit = async () => {
  setStatus('pending');
  await api.createPayment(cart.id);
  setStatus('success');
};
return <button onClick={onSubmit}>Pay</button>;
```
The button has no disabled state tied to status, so Submit remains enabled while the first request is pending. tests/PayButton.test.tsx:40 double-clicks and logs `createPayment calls: 2`, so the handler accepts a second event that creates a duplicate payment. Recovery expectation: one payment per submission, with a retry offered only after an error.
